ci's own run programs (doc/C23-SURVEY.md, "As built: review 006's fixes"; test/c/corpora.edn's :ci-run): each file a
program with a main, a case one of ci's back ends (the interpreter, cf2g's compiled Go) once got wrong, judged as the
run corpora are: bin/ci record-ref --corpus ci-run --only records gcc 15.2's -O0 run into test/c/ref-gcc15.edn, then
bin/ci check --corpus ci-run and bin/ci check --aot --corpus ci-run. Arbace's own, under the EPL-1.0 (LICENSE.md).

- ptr-sub-unsigned.c, ptr-sub-narrow.c: pointer minus an integer narrower than 64 bits (unsigned int, unsigned char,
  unsigned short, _Bool, signed char's minimum), review 006's finding 2.
- nan-to-unsigned.c: a NaN converted to unsigned long and unsigned int (gcc -O0's comisd 2^63 is unordered, so its
  plain cvttsd2si gives 0x8000000000000000), review 006's finding 10.
- builtin-bitg.c, builtin-stdc.c: gcc's type-generic bit builtins (popcountg, parityg, clzg, ctzg, ffsg, clrsbg)
  and C23's <stdbit.h> builtins (__builtin_stdc_*) over the standard types, unsigned __int128 and _BitInt narrow and
  wide, their result types and their folding, queue 126.
- builtin-overflow-p.c: __builtin_add_overflow_p, sub_overflow_p and mul_overflow_p, narrow and wide, signed and
  unsigned operands mixed, the third argument's effects once, their folding; the storing forms on wide types, queue 126.
- builtin-fpclass-fl.c: __builtin_isinff, isinfl, isnanf, isnanl, finitef, finitel (no LDBL_MAX: long double is
  double, CS35), queue 126.
- builtin-atomic.c: gcc's __atomic_* and __sync_* builtins (the _n and generic forms, every read-modify-write, compare-exchange,
  test-and-set, the fences) and fmodf and fmodl, LLS21 (a).
- fnptr-result-width.c: a call through a function pointer reads the result at the pointer's return type (qsort's comparator
  that returns unsigned, a long read as int, an int read as unsigned char), LLS21 (a), the llvmi row's abi-punning.
- builtin-lockfree.c: __atomic_is_lock_free, __atomic_always_lock_free and atomic_is_lock_free for sizes 1 to 8,
  queue 126.
- builtin-assoc-barrier.c: __builtin_assoc_barrier over _BitInt(255), double and narrow operands, queue 126.
- builtin-clear-padding.c: __builtin_clear_padding over structures with padding, bit-fields (unnamed, zero-width),
  a union, nested and anonymous members and arrays, queue 126.
- vla-types.c: variably modified types at run time (queue 165): sizeof of a VLA typedef and through a pointer to a
  VLA, pointer arithmetic and subscripts over VLA rows, a parameter's array size evaluated at entry with its effects,
  an unnamed parameter (its argument was dropped), a pointer-to-VLA parameter, typeof and auto of a variably modified
  type, a VLA's empty initializer.
- vla-struct.c: GNU's structures and unions with variably modified members (CS106, 2026-11-06): their layout at run
  time where the definition stands (packed, a union, nested), sizeof and offsetof, members after one of variable
  size, copies, arrays of them and pointers stepping by them, one passed through varargs.
- complex-int.c: GNU's complex integer types (CS105, 2026-11-06): +, -, *, / (gcc's wide method with integer
  division), the part types' wrapping, conversions to and from floating complex and scalar types, equality, truth,
  negation, conjugation.
- signal-sync.c: synchronous faults delivered to the program's handlers (review 006's signals, 2026-11-06): SIGFPE
  twice through siglongjmp, SIGSEGV to an SA_SIGINFO handler, then SIG_DFL ending the run with 136.
- va-arg-pack.c: __builtin_va_arg_pack and __builtin_va_arg_pack_len (CS277, 2026-11-06): always_inline variadic
  functions forwarding their variadic arguments (integers, doubles, strings, none) to variadic callees and printf.
